<title>NEW ZEALAND: Cheetham Salt cleared to buy 50 pct of Dominion NZ.</title>
<headline>Cheetham Salt cleared to buy 50 pct of Dominion NZ.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand Commerce Commission said on Thursday it had granted clearance for Ridley Corp Ltd's Cheetham Salt to acquire around a half interest in the Dominion Salt group of companies.</p>
<p>Cheetham proposes to buy Skellerup Group Ltd's shares in Dominion.</p>
<p>Cerebos Gregg's Ltd would continue to own the remaining shares in Dominion. Cerebos Greggs is a unit of Cerebos Pacific.</p>
<p>Ridley said in August it would buy half share for NZ$36 million.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
